hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1049","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My heirs should not distribute even a single dinar from my estate; after providing for my wives' expenses and the expenses of the one who manages my property, whatever remains should be given in charity."""
"1050","Through another chain, a narration with the same meaning as the previous hadith is reported from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1051","It is narrated from Buraidah Al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ): ""I gave a slave in charity on behalf of my mother, and now she has passed away."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Your charity has become obligatory, and it is your inheritance."""
"1052","Abdullah bin Hasan bin Husayn narrates from several members of the household of the Prophet (peace be upon him). Muhammad bin Ali says, I think he mentioned Zaid bin Ali, that Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), gave her wealth in charity to Banu Hashim and Banu Muttalib, so Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) distributed the charity among them and also gave to others along with them."
"1053","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the Prophet (ﷺ) came, bread and a household dish were placed before him. He (ﷺ) said: ""Did I not see a pot of meat (on the stove)?"" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""This was given in charity to Barirah."" He (ﷺ) said: ""It is charity for her and a gift for us."""
"1054","Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated that I was with Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) when a man from among the Bedouins came and said, ""I had gifted a she-camel to my son for as long as he lived, and she bore many camels."" So Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""That she-camel belongs to him, whether he lives or dies."" The man said: ""I had given it as charity."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""If that is the case, then you cannot take it back under any circumstance."""
"1055","It is narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Habib bin Abi Thabit, but in this narration, he added these words: that she gave birth to a child and they were restless."
"1056","Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated that we were with Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) when a Bedouin came and said: ""I have given one of my sons a she-camel for as long as he lives."" Amr said in the narration: ""And it bore many offspring,"" and Ibn Abi Najih said in his narration: ""Rather, it had many offspring and they became restless."" Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said: ""The she-camel belongs to him, whether it lives or dies."" The man said: ""But I had given it to him as charity."" He replied: ""Then you cannot take it back under any circumstance."""
"1057","It is narrated from Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) that his father brought him to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: “I have given this son of mine a slave as a gift.” The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked: “Have you given a similar slave to your other sons as well?” He replied: “No.” Thereupon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Then take it back from him.” Abu al-Abbas stated that all of our companions have this narration through Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him), so I have narrated it with some doubt."
"1058","It is narrated from Tawus that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""It is not lawful for one who gives a gift to take back what he has given, except for a father who gives to his son (he may take it back)."""
"1059","It is narrated from Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them) who said: My mother came to me during the time of the Quraysh and she was not a Muslim. I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) whether I should maintain ties of kinship with her. He (ﷺ) said: ""Yes."""
"1060","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a (silk) cloak of Sira at the door of the mosque and said: O Messenger of Allah! If you would buy this, you could wear it on Fridays and when delegations come to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only he who has no share in the Hereafter can wear this."" Then several cloaks of the same kind came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he gave one of those cloaks to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! You have given this to me even though you previously said what you said about the cloak of Atarid? (i.e., you forbade wearing it). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I did not give it to you so that you would wear it."" So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent it to his polytheist brother in Mecca for him to wear."
